      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This observation relates an exceptional case of gastrointestinal myiasis in a 15 year-old rural Moroccan girl. She was admitted for abdominal pain, hematemesis, and worm vomitting. The parasitologic identification revealed Sarcophaga hemorrhoidalis. Through this observation, the authors underline the epidemiological, clinical and evolutive aspects of this parasitosis in Morocco."},
